WEBVTT

00:00.800 --> 00:04.800
TorchBearer is an AI apprentice that captures how experts really work,

00:04.800 --> 00:09.840
maps it, and teaches it to the next person. First, in the capture step, the expert works

00:09.840 --> 00:15.200
as usual while TorchBearer watches, and at natural pauses, an ElevenLabs voice agent

00:15.200 --> 00:20.320
asks about the reasoning behind each step. Why this step? Is there a limit? When would you

00:20.320 --> 00:24.480
stop and ask someone? The expert just talks through it the way they would explain it to a new

00:24.480 --> 00:30.320
colleague. Let's take a look. I'm going to launch it right now and tell it that we're going to do a

00:30.320 --> 00:38.560
food expense learning today. And then I share the entire screen and it starts to capture.

00:40.960 --> 00:46.560
Hi Paul, I'm TorchBearer. Go ahead and show me how you submit your expenses. I'll stay quiet

00:46.560 --> 00:52.720
and only ask when you pause. Does the system always split costs equally when adding a guest?

00:52.720 --> 00:58.080
Originally it does, but you can adjust the percentages yourself.

01:00.400 --> 01:02.320
Understood. You can adjust it.

01:04.480 --> 01:09.280
When the expert finishes, TorchBearer then explains the whole process back in its own words,

01:09.280 --> 01:14.320
and the expert corrects anything you got wrong until it's right. The result is a Work Map.

01:14.320 --> 01:20.000
Every step, rule, and guardrail linked to the exact screen moment and the expert's own words.

01:20.320 --> 01:25.600
New hires then get coached by TorchBearer on this workflow or any recorded before it. It asks them

01:25.600 --> 01:29.920
to predict the next step, gives them hints when they're stuck, and stops them before they break

01:29.920 --> 01:34.720
a guardrail, explaining why in the expert's own words. Based on what you saw earlier,

01:34.720 --> 01:45.760
what do you need besides the receipt? An invoice? That's a good thought, but for delivery orders,

01:45.840 --> 01:52.080
Paul always makes sure to include something else. Think about what confirms the delivery itself.

01:53.200 --> 01:54.480
A delivery confirmation?

01:56.240 --> 02:02.080
Spot on! A delivery confirmation is exactly what Paul includes for these types of orders.

